    title: "go: net.Conn.Write / net.Conn.Read are single-rowed (net_send / net_recv) and read no io_target_kind, so a write or read through a Unix-domain connection's OWN method is still a network crossing after WI-potog -- WI-baran's dual-row half, for Go's method form"  # 6992
